<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yelü Chucai</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1190">1190</a>–<a href="/years/1244">1244</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Yelü Chucai was a Khitan statesman of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liao-dynasty">Liao</a> royal line who served <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genghis-khan">Genghis Khan</a> and Ögedei as adviser and administrator. He persuaded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a> to tax the conquered farmlands of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> rather than turn them into pasture, organised a regular tax system with a Chinese-style bureaucracy and protected Confucian scholars. His influence waned in Ögedei's last years.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/yelu-chucai.jpg" alt="Yelü Chucai" width="320" height="424" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gisling · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E8%80%B6%E5%BE%8B%E6%A5%9A%E6%9D%90.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
